  "body": "Exact frame audits repeatedly compute row GCDs in Python and rebuild the ambient-form action during complement checks. Use variadic `math.gcd`, compute `Ga = 9a-sum(a)*1` once per current row, and reuse those exact covectors for construction and verification. Dimension and orthogonality checks remain; inconsistent input widths now fail explicitly. No additional cache or dependency is introduced.\n\nThis follows Richard Hoekstra's incorporated #239. Only `scripts/rational_span_frames.py` and `tests/test_rational_span_frames.py` change. Exact arithmetic, selected frames, dirty-input obligations and the multiplication exponent are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nPinned base: `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`. Final upstream check: `49b3157d1d89adcef16df8be98445451672be5ba`; among original `scripts/` and `tests/` files only the unrelated research-assignment helper and its tests changed. The affected code and test inputs retain their pinned bytes.\n\n- Baseline: **40 tests pass**. Patched: **42 tests pass**, covering rational frames, mixed-point, block-carry, joint-return, early-sharing/center and physical stage-pair behavior.\n- New controls check integer normalization, direct Fraction-oracle decisions, complement rank and the original ambient-form equations, malformed widths and forged kernel results.\n- The patch applies to a fresh public-source copy; whitespace checks pass.\n- Five fresh processes per arm execute the unchanged complete h=10/h=12 mixed-point benchmark, on one CPU with nice 15, a 4 GiB address-space limit, Linux x86_64 and CPython 3.10.12. Filesystem caches were not flushed.\n\n| Paired sample | Baseline audit seconds | Patched audit seconds | Baseline peak RSS KiB | Patched peak RSS KiB |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 3.352190758 | 2.710022644 | 95,600 | 95,676 |\n| 2 | 3.103290897 | 2.636687679 | 95,744 | 95,752 |\n| 3 | 2.972289573 | 3.125113534 | 95,604 | 95,832 |\n| 4 | 3.215038218 | 3.043583594 | 95,672 | 95,716 |\n| 5 | 4.147957690 | 4.019752780 | 95,548 | 95,672 |\n| Median | 3.215038218 | 3.043583594 | 95,604 | 95,716 |\n\nExecution order was baseline/patched, patched/baseline, baseline/patched, patched/baseline, baseline/patched. Median audit time falls **5.33%**; median total process time falls **5.12%** (3.378918 to 3.206012 seconds). Samples overlap, and one pair regresses. This is a local measurement on these customers, not a hardware-independent or multiplication-runtime speed claim.\n\nAll ten complete mathematical payloads and selected-frame digests agree exactly, SHA256 `faa0f9c0159a6e70d4e2cfcdb4012ea62ef350bd26b81312d11da4a770f8b218`. All original baseline inputs remain unchanged. An earlier test invocation stopped before collection because its working directory was wrong; it is excluded from the qualification.\n\nReproduce the affected tests with unittest discovery for the six named modules. For a fresh timing sample, use the same unchanged benchmark script against each source tree:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B tests/benchmark_rational_span_frames.py BASE NEW_BASE_RESULT.json --cpu CPU\npython3 -B tests/benchmark_rational_span_frames.py PATCHED NEW_PATCHED_RESULT.json --cpu CPU\n```\n\nRun every sample in a new process with matching external limits. Full historical `make verify`, selected-supplier cold replay and hosted CI were not run: this change does not alter the selected supplier or its artifacts. No native or Lean build is involved.\n\nDeveloped with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance.\n",
